.TH XPUB\-ADDRESSES 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.1" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
xpub\-addresses \- extended public key (xpub/ypub/zpub/tpub..., stdin, one per line) \-> watch\-only
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
xpub\-addresses [\-\-chain btc] [\-\-kind p2wpkh,..] [\-\-change 0,1] [\-\-count 20] < xpub \-> address lines
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
addresses. No secrets in or out: an xpub can't sign, so nothing found here can be swept.
.nf
.RS 2
  xpub\-addresses [\-\-chain btc] [\-\-kind p2wpkh,...] [\-\-change 0,1] [\-\-count 20]
.RE
.fi
Paths in the output are relative to the xpub (m/{change}/{i}); only non\-hardened steps exist.
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
\-\-chain
\-\-change
\-\-count
\-\-kind
.fi
Each flag's meaning is in the SYNOPSIS usage line(s) above (taken from \-\-help).
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
xpub\-addresses: extended public key (xpub/ypub/zpub/tpub..., stdin, one per line) \-> watch\-only
addresses. No secrets in or out: an xpub can't sign, so nothing found here can be swept.
Paths in the output are relative to the xpub (m/{change}/{i}); only non\-hardened steps exist.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
0
last status done
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
